  "reviewer_note": "Local trade is older than 130 BCE, and sources end the routes at different dates (WHE 1453; UNESCO the 16th century). The drawn line is one main route, not the whole network: UW Silk Road Seattle also describes a southern route by Miran, Niya and Khotan, and branches to India. Between Merv and Antioch no source opened names the stops; the line there bends through Iran and Mesopotamia on route-shape points only. Kucha is placed at GeoNames' Xincheng (alt. Kuqa).",
